---
/** /about/ — positioning, beliefs and boundaries. Copy carried over from the
 *  previous build unchanged; no team names or headcount are asserted, because
 *  none have been supplied. */
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import NextBand from '../components/NextBand.astro';
import { SITE } from '../consts';
import { ALL_SERVICES } from '../services';

const beliefs = [
  {
    title: 'A figure without a derivation is an opinion',
    body:
      'If you cannot show how a number was produced, you are asking someone to trust you rather than to check you. Every figure our systems produce keeps a path back to the entries behind it.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Judgement belongs to people',
    body:
      'Software should remove the mechanical work and hand the decisions back, clearly framed. A system that quietly takes tax positions on your behalf has moved risk without moving responsibility.',
  },
  {
    title: 'The printed version is the real one',
    body:
      'What gets filed, signed and defended is usually a document. We design for paper as deliberately as for screen, because that is the artefact that outlives the session.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Local regimes are not configuration',
    body:
      'UAE Corporate Tax is not a checkbox on a global product. Free zone qualifying income, de minimis tests and the evidentiary expectations here need to be built in, not mapped onto something designed elsewhere.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Boring software wins',
    body:
      'Finance tooling should be predictable, legible and slightly dull. Novelty in an accounting system is a cost you pay at year-end.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Say the difficult thing early',
    body:
      'If your ledger will not support what you want, or the project is larger than you hoped, that is a first-call conversation. Discovering it in month three serves nobody.',
  },
];

const boundaries = [
  {
    title: 'Not your auditor',
    body:
      'We are accounting and tax consultants. A firm that prepares the records cannot independently audit them, so we do not audit clients whose books we keep. We will work alongside your auditor and prepare the year-end file for them.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Not a law firm',
    body:
      'Tax has legal edges, and some questions belong with a lawyer. We will say when you have reached one rather than answering outside what we are qualified to answer.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Not an advice channel on this website',
    body:
      'We do advise — under a signed engagement letter. Nothing on this site is advice, and no advisory relationship arises from reading it or from using the estimator. That distinction protects you as much as us.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Not a replacement for your ledger',
    body:
      'The platform reads your accounting system; it does not replace it. If you are choosing bookkeeping software, that decision comes before us and we are happy to be left out of it.',
  },
];
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="NUMARATECH is a UAE accounting and tax consultancy that also builds the platform it works on — why we exist, what we believe, and where the boundaries are."
  ownNav={true}
>
  <PageHero
    kicker="About / Dubai, United Arab Emirates"
    title="A practice that builds its own tools."
    lead="Between the accounting system and the filing there is a gap that has always been filled by a spreadsheet and somebody's memory. We advise in that gap, and we build the software that closes it."
    primary={{ label: 'Talk to the practice', href: '/contact/' }}
    secondary={{ label: 'See the platform', href: '/platform/' }}
    stats={[
      { label: 'Practice', value: 'accounting and tax consultants' },
      { label: 'Service lines', value: String(ALL_SERVICES.length) },
      { label: 'Base', value: `${SITE.address.city}, ${SITE.address.country}` },
      { label: 'Platform', value: 'two live, four at idea stage' },
    ]}
  />

  <section class="nt-section">
    <div class="nt-eyebrow"><b>01</b><span>Why</span></div>
    <h2 class="nt-h2">Where this came from.</h2>
    <div class="nt-split--even nt-split">
      <div>
        <p class="nt-body">
          The UAE introduced Corporate Tax for financial years beginning on or after 1 June 2023.
          Overnight, a large number of businesses that had never needed a defensible tax computation
          needed one every year.
        </p>
        <p class="nt-small">
          What most of them had was an accounting system that produced a trial balance, and a
          workbook that turned that trial balance into whatever was needed. The workbook was built by
          one capable person, was understood by that person, and was correct — until the person
          changed, the business grew, or somebody asked how a figure had been derived eighteen months
          earlier.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="nt-small">
          We started NUMARATECH because that pattern does not scale and does not survive scrutiny.
          The answer is not a bigger workbook or a global ERP with an Emirates module bolted to the
          side. It is a thin, specific layer that maps the ledger once and derives everything else
          from it.
        </p>
        <p class="nt-small">
          So the business has two halves, and we keep them separate on purpose. We are a
          <a class="nt-link" href="/advisory/">licensed accounting and tax consultancy</a> — engaged
          under an engagement letter, forming judgements, accountable for the advice. And we build
          the <a class="nt-link" href="/platform/">platform</a> our own team uses to do that work,
          which we license to other firms and finance functions.
        </p>
        <p class="nt-small">
          Each half makes the other honest. The software is shaped by people who have to file with
          it; the advice is faster and more defensible because the tooling underneath it was built
          for exactly this. Neither is a side project of the other, and you can buy either one alone.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="nt-section nt-dark nt-dark--navy nt-section--flush">
    <div class="nt-grid--v"></div>
    <div class="nt-layer">
      <div class="nt-eyebrow"><b>02</b><span>What we believe</span></div>
      <h2 class="nt-h2">Six positions that shape the product.</h2>
      <p class="nt-body">
        Not values on a wall. Each of these has cost us a feature request we chose not to build.
      </p>
      <div class="nt-cells nt-cells--3" style="--nt-cols:3">
        {
          beliefs.map((belief, i) => (
            <div class="nt-cell">
              <div class="nt-cell__num">{String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</div>
              <h3 class="nt-h3">{belief.title}</h3>
              <p>{belief.body}</p>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="nt-section">
    <div class="nt-eyebrow"><b>03</b><span>Boundaries</span></div>
    <h2 class="nt-h2">What we are not.</h2>
    <p class="nt-body">Being explicit about this saves everybody a wasted meeting.</p>
    <div class="nt-cells" style="--nt-cols:2">
      {
        boundaries.map((boundary) => (
          <div class="nt-cell">
            <h3 class="nt-h3">{boundary.title}</h3>
            <p>{boundary.body}</p>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="nt-section">
    <div class="nt-eyebrow"><b>04</b><span>Working with us</span></div>
    <h2 class="nt-h2">What the first call is like.</h2>
    <div class="nt-split--even nt-split">
      <div>
        <p class="nt-body">Thirty minutes, your numbers on screen, no deck.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="nt-small">
          We will ask what your ledger looks like, how last year's computation was produced, and who
          holds the knowledge. By the end of it you will have a direct answer on whether we can help,
          roughly what it would take, and what we think the real problem is — which is not always the
          one you called about.
        </p>
        <p class="nt-small">
          If the honest answer is that you do not need us yet, that is the answer you will get.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <NextBand
    title="Have the first conversation."
    body="Bring one entity, one period, and the workbook you currently rely on. That is enough for both of us to know whether this is worth continuing."
  />
</Base>
